{"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/ClientProfile\/unknown","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK","doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/ClientProfile"]]},"kind":"symbol","metadata":{"externalID":"s:8AxiamSDK13ClientProfileO7unknownyA2CmF","roleHeading":"Case","role":"symbol","symbolKind":"case","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"case"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"unknown"}],"modules":[{"name":"AxiamSDK"}],"title":"ClientProfile.unknown"},"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"minor":3,"major":0},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"case","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"unknown","kind":"identifier"}],"platforms":["Linux"]}]}],"sections":[],"abstract":[{"text":"A value this SDK’s copy of the spec does not list; see the type’s summary.","type":"text"}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/axiamsdk\/clientprofile\/unknown"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"references":{"Self::Standard":{"titleInlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Standard"}],"identifier":"Self::Standard","url":"Self::Standard","title":"Standard","type":"link"},"doc://AxiamSDK/documentation/AxiamSDK/ClientProfile/unknown":{"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"case","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"unknown","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"text":"A value this SDK’s copy of the spec does not list; see the type’s summary.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/ClientProfile\/unknown","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/axiamsdk\/clientprofile\/unknown","title":"ClientProfile.unknown","type":"topic"},"doc://AxiamSDK/documentation/AxiamSDK":{"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/axiamsdk","role":"collection","identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK","abstract":[{"text":"The official Swift SDK for AXIAM (Access eXtended Identity and Authorization Management).","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","title":"AxiamSDK"},"doc://AxiamSDK/documentation/AxiamSDK/ClientProfile":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/ClientProfile","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"ClientProfile","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"enum","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"ClientProfile","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Which security posture a client is registered under (X5.1). This is the FAPI “one switch”."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"FAPI 2.0 is not a single feature but a bundle of constraints — mandatory PAR, mandatory PKCE"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"with "},{"code":"S256","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", mandatory strong client authentication, mandatory sender-constrained tokens,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and a refusal of every relaxation the base specs permit. Encoding them as one profile rather"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"than a dozen independent booleans means an operator cannot register a client that is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"nearly"}]},{"type":"text","text":" FAPI, and a reviewer can answer “is this client financial-grade?” by reading one"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"field. The same philosophy as the rate-limit postures: ordinary clients see no behaviour"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"change at all, because "},{"identifier":"Self::Standard","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" is the serde default and every row"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"written before schema v38 decodes to it."}],"title":"ClientProfile","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/axiamsdk\/clientprofile"}}}